! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routine IBN-IBN11, p.35 (octal 004523.40-004550.40),
! with its constants at 004512.00-004523.00 from p.34:
! %V+ICR%, ADD TO VALUE IMMEDIATE, COUNT + REFILL.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  V+ICR's REFILL PATH was one of the five index
! operations the suite was measured not to reach.  Every other
! progressive-index block in the suite either never counts down to
! zero or was written to avoid the refill; this one is the listing's
! own refill test and it does nothing else.
!
! THE FIRST TEST IS THE WHOLE POINT, and it is three instructions long.
! IBM61 holds value IBN+.4, COUNT 1, REFILL IBM70.  One V+ICR takes
! the count to zero, which forces the refill, so X1 is no longer the
! word that was loaded -- it is IBM70's word.  SX then stores that
! word over IBN1.  IBM70's word is NOT an index word at all: it is
! "NOP,0" followed by "BD,IBN3", TWO VALID INSTRUCTIONS, which is what
! the listing means by "IBN1 SHOULD NOW BE TWO VALID OP".  Execution
! falls straight into them and carries on.  Without the refill IBN1
! stays "BE,$" and the machine hangs on a branch to itself.
!
! A refill that fetched the right word into the wrong fields would not
! survive either: the stored word has to be IBM70's word EXACTLY, bit
! for bit, because it is being executed.
!
! THE SECOND TEST checks the opposite case -- a V+ICR whose count does
! NOT reach zero -- and it checks all three fields separately, each
! through the same trick of manufacturing a branch:
!
!   V  stored straight into IBN5, which must then branch to 004537.40
!      ("BD,IBN6"), stepping over the BD,$ at 004537.00.
!   C  round-tripped through ISTOY (SC then LV, which multiplies it by
!      64), added to IBM76's dummy address, stored into IBN8: count 1
!      lands on 004543.40, count 2 would land a word further on.
!   R  round-tripped the same way through SR, added to IBM77's 1.4,
!      stored into IBN9: refill IBN9 gives 004547.00, IBN10.
!
! So the block proves that ONE V+ICR decremented the count by exactly
! one, left the refill field alone, and added exactly 2.0 to the
! value -- with three independent branches, not one combined check.
!
! Note IBM62's value is written IBN4+.36 and IBM61's IBN+.4: those bit
! offsets are DECIMAL (.36 prints as .44 octal), unlike the explicitly
! octal (8).04 of the neighbouring routines.

        SLC, (8)6105.0
ISTOY   DD(BU,64,8), 0

        SLC, (8)4512.0
IBM61   XW, IBN+.4, 1, IBM70                 ! XW for V+ICR tests
IBM62   XW, IBN4+.36, 2, IBN9
IBM63   XW, 0, 0, 0                          ! temp IX wd storage
IBM64   XW, 0, 0, 0
IBM65   XW, 0, 0, 0
IBM70   NOP, 0
        BD, IBN3
IBM71   BE, 0                                ! count storage area
IBM72   BE, 0                                ! refill storage area
IBM73   BE, 0                                ! temp V storage
IBM74   BE, 0                                ! temp C storage
IBM75   BE, 0                                ! temp R storage
IBM76   VF, IBN8+(8).04                      ! dummy address, see IBN6
IBM77   VF, 1.4                              ! one word and 4 bits
IBN     LX, $X1, IBM61                       ! start V+ICR tests
        V+ICR, $X1, 2.0                      ! V was IBN+.4, C was 1, R was IBM70
        SX, $X1, IBN1                        ! IBN1 should now be two valid op
        NOP, 0                               ! space for store close to
        CNOP                                 ! instruct fetch interlock
IBN1    BE, $                                ! becomes NOP,0
        BE, $                                ! becomes BD,IBN3
IBN2    BD, $
IBN3    LX, $X1, IBM62                       ! start next test
        V+ICR, $X1, 2.0                      ! C was 2, so no refill
        SX, $X1, IBM63                       ! V is IBN4+.4+, C is 1, R is IBN9
        SV, $X1, IBM73                       ! temp storage, V is
        SV, $X1, IBN5
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        SV, $X1, IBM74                       ! C is 1
        SR, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        SV, $X1, IBM75                       ! R is IBN9
IBN4    NOP, 0
        LV, $X1, IBM73
        NOP, 0
IBN5    BE, $                                ! becomes BD, IBN4+2.4 if V correct
        BD, $
        BD, IBN6                             ! to test count field
        BD, $
IBN6    LV, $X1, IBM76                       ! test count field for 1
        V+, $X1, IBM74
IBN7    SV, $X1, IBN8
        NOP, 0
IBN8    BE, $                                ! becomes BD,IBN8+1 if count correct
        NOP
        LV, $X1, IBM75                       ! test refill field
        V+, $X1, IBM77
        SV, $X1, IBN9
        NOP, 0
        NOP, 0
IBN9    BE, $                                ! becomes BD,IBN10 if refill unchanged
        BD, $
IBN10   BD, IBN11                            ! to skip over V+ICR on this modi-
        NOP, 0                               ! fied IX word because now the same
        NOP, -1                              ! as the first test.
IBN11   NOP, 0.0
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBN
